{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Your burden.</b> In quarrelsomeness that does not involve monetary claims." "<b>And your load.</b> In the needs of the many." "<b>And your strife.</b> In matters of judgment and monetary claims. He recounted this to remind them of their transgression: even though he had told them they would enter the Land without any war — a matter of surpassing benefit and honor, more than all their possessions and affairs in the wilderness — they did not refrain from stirring up disputes, one man against another, so that it became necessary to appoint tiers of judges until every ten of them required a private judge. This was nothing but evil of heart."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:03.218357364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}